  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "When deploying fcrepo-camel in karaf, it is possible to copy the compiled jarfile to the $KARAF_HOME/deploy folder, but it would be better to have a features.xml artifact in the maven repository so that you can add (provision) fcrepo-camel support to karaf like you can with other camel artifacts. This is described here: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://karaf.apache.org/manual/latest/users-guide/provisioning.html"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://karaf.apache.org/manual/latest/users-guide/provisioning.html",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Basically, with a features.xml file, deployment consists of:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "> feature:repo-add mvn:org.fcrepo.camel/fcrepo-camel/4.0.1/xml/features",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> feature:install fcrepo-camel",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This would make deployment of fcrepo-camel-based routes significantly easier.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
